.TH GUI 1 "October 2026" "gui 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gui \- terminal text editor with a classic menu interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gui
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B gui --help
.br
.B gui --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gui
edits UTF-8 text in a color terminal using keyboard shortcuts, menus,
and mouse input.  It can keep up to nine documents open and display
two editing panels with independent cursor and scroll positions.
.PP
An optional
.I file
is opened at startup.  A nonexistent path starts a new document at that path.
Only one file argument is accepted; use the Open menu to open more documents.
Without an argument, gui starts with a blank document.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display the version, usage and main shortcuts, then exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display the version and brief usage information, then exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.BR Ctrl+N ", " Ctrl+O ", " Ctrl+S
Create a document, open a file, or save the active document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit, asking about unsaved changes in every open document.
.TP
.B Shift+arrows
Select text while moving the cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all text in the active document.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+C " or " Ctrl+Insert
Copy the selection to gui's internal clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+X
Cut the selection to the internal clipboard.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+V " or " Shift+Insert
Paste from the internal clipboard.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Z ", " Ctrl+Y
Undo or redo changes in the active document.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+B ", " Ctrl+R ", " F3
Find text, replace text, or repeat the last search.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+F6 ", " Ctrl+F8 ", " Ctrl+F4
Split, resize, or close an editing window.
.TP
.B F6
Switch panels, or switch to the next document when only one panel is visible.
.TP
.B Alt+1 through Alt+9
Switch documents.
.TP
.B F10
Open the menu bar.  Navigate menus with the arrow keys and Enter.
.TP
.B F1
Open About gui.
.PP
Alt+F, Alt+E, Alt+S, Alt+V, Alt+O and Alt+H open File, Edit, Search,
View, Options and Help, respectively.  Alt+A, Alt+B and Alt+Y are aliases
for File, Search and Help.
.PP
In dialogs, Tab and Shift+Tab change focus, Space toggles checkboxes,
Enter activates a control, and a single Esc cancels the current dialog.
In Open, Enter on a selected file opens it immediately; Enter on a directory
navigates into it.  Menu commands are available
when the terminal intercepts a shortcut.  Alt alone is not detectable in
terminals that send no input for it.
.SH MOUSE
Click to place the cursor or activate a menu or control.  Hold the left
button and drag to select text, then use a copy or cut shortcut.
.SH CLIPBOARD
The clipboard is internal to gui and shared between its documents.
It does not write selections to the desktop clipboard.
To paste from another application, use the terminal's paste command.
Bracketed terminal paste is supported in the document editing area.
.SH WINDOWS
Split Window creates another view of the current document.  Choose a
document from View to display a different document in the active panel.
Use F6 or a mouse click to switch panels.
.PP
Size Window adjusts the divider with Up and Down or with the left mouse
button held.  Enter accepts the new size and Esc cancels.
At least 12 terminal rows are needed for two panels.
.PP
Closing one of two panels keeps its document open.  Closing the sole
panel closes its document after checking for unsaved changes.
Closing the last document creates a blank document.
.SH SETTINGS
Options/Settings controls tab spacing, from 1 to 32 columns.
Options/Colors controls foreground and background colors.
Accepted preferences are saved per user; no global configuration is required.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gui/settings
Preferences when XDG_CONFIG_HOME names an absolute directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gui/settings
Preferences when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or is not an absolute path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal capabilities used by ncurses.  gui does not substitute another profile.
.TP
.B ESCDELAY
Milliseconds allowed to distinguish Esc from a terminal key sequence.
gui defaults to 50 when this variable is unset.  An explicit value is
respected; a larger value may help on slow connections but delays Esc.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
Locale settings.  A UTF-8 locale, such as C.UTF-8, is required for editing.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " HOME
Determine the per-user preferences directory.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Text must be valid UTF-8 without NUL bytes.  The UTF-8 byte-order mark
and uniform LF or CRLF line endings are preserved; mixed line endings
are normalized to CRLF if any CRLF is present.
.PP
Open Binary provides a read-only hexadecimal view, not binary editing.
Its Line Width setting is bytes per row, from 1 to 256.
Search is literal, without regular expressions.
Saving over symbolic links is not supported.
.PP
Documents and up to 64 undo snapshots per document are held in memory.
The editor is intended for small and medium files.
Editing uses Unicode code points, not full grapheme clusters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, including help and version display.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or a fatal startup or allocation error.
.PP
Nonfatal editing and file-operation errors are reported inside the editor.
